questionAnswers.Q0:
F1, F2, F5, F6 and F7 are CLOSED. F3 is PARTIAL (R2-F2, R2-F3). F4 is CLOSED in the text, with a residual model gap (R2-F4).
No mutator can still change an image volume. AlwaysPullImages' only other target, container pull policy, is pinned by A2-POD-PULL-POLICY.
Other fields outside the disposition tables do still change while A2 admits:
- pod-level resource defaulting;
- the matchLabelKeys and mismatchLabelKeys selector merges;
- the env fieldRef and fileKeyRef defaults;
- disabled-gate field drops.
All are deterministic functions of the admitted manifest under the pinned W02g gates, so none is a cluster-state lever (R2-F1, R2-F2).
The root-CA exemption is bound exactly to the name kube-root-ca.crt and the identity system:serviceaccount:kube-system:root-ca-cert-publisher, which is the real publisher identity under --use-service-account-credentials. Its shape matches the publisher's real object. It is slightly looser than 'exactly' for that identity (R2-F5), not over-broad.

questionAnswers.Q2:
The plugin rows are complete for the W02g allowlist. I re-read Admit at the pinned commit, and the digests match:
- ServiceAccount (admission.go:137-177);
- Priority (admitPod, establishPriority; a globalDefault always sets priorityClassName);
- LimitRanger (mergeContainerResources always sets the kubernetes.io/limit-ranger annotation when it sets anything, :236-291);
- DefaultTolerationSeconds;
- AlwaysPullImages (:61-84, containers and image volumes);
- RuntimeClass and PodTopologyLabels, gated by forbidden fields.
The new 1.37 plugins (PodGroupProtection, NodeDeclaredFeatureValidator, PodResizeValidator) do not mutate Pods on CREATE.
Gaps:
- PrepareForCreate and defaulting rows that are listed with FIXED values but have no disposition (R2-F1): pod-level resources (strategy.go:101, util.go:2253-2278), the matchLabelKeys and mismatchLabelKeys merges (strategy.go:98-99), and the env defaults;
- the disabled-gate drop, which is not enforced by the reference signer check (R2-F2).
The AppArmor annotation-to-field sync (strategy.go:975-1029) is ruled out in effect by MC04, because the annotation key is reserved. ConfigMap and Service rows agree with the code as read.

questionAnswers.Q3:
Within the closed mutator set, I found no cluster-state lever that changes the persisted object beyond the documented or deterministic deltas while every A2 validation passes:
- ServiceAccount pull secrets and automount: E05, E12;
- a globalDefault PriorityClass: E06;
- LimitRange: E07, by annotation;
- toleration flags: E09;
- service CIDR and family: E10, E11;
- AlwaysPullImages with image volumes: U05, now refused;
- RuntimeClass and Node labels: gated by MC30.
The residual undispositioned deltas (R2-F1, R2-F2) are deterministic functions of the A1-admitted bytes under the W02g-pinned gates. They are completeness gaps, not bypasses.
The shape echo argument is sound and its bound is stated: a mutator that rewrote a field and its echo together would have to be outside W02g SC05 and OR06.
The guarantee depends on the signer, and C25 now says so. It is incomplete for disabled-gate fields (R2-F2).
The publisher exemption admits nothing from any other identity, and nothing from the publisher under another name.

questionAnswers.Q6:
